---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="LinkedIn Copy Kit - Robertas Rudys"
  description="Copy-paste LinkedIn text blocks for Robertas Rudys."
>
  <h1>LinkedIn Copy Kit</h1>
  <p><a class="touch-link" href="/">Back to homepage</a></p>
  <p>
    Primary profile lives on this site. LinkedIn is a distribution channel
    mirror.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Last updated:</strong>
    <time datetime={lastUpdated}>{lastUpdated}</time>
  </p>

  <section aria-labelledby="sync-checklist-heading">
    <h2 id="sync-checklist-heading">Quick Sync Checklist</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Open this page and LinkedIn edit mode in separate tabs.</li>
      <li>Update this page first if positioning or wording changed.</li>
      <li>
        Copy headline, about, featured section, and top role bullets to
        LinkedIn.
      </li>
      <li>Save LinkedIn.</li>
      <li>
        If LinkedIn forces edits, apply those edits here and re-copy from this
        page.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="headline-heading">
    <h2 id="headline-heading">1. Headline</h2>
    <div class="copy-block">
      <button
        class="copy-button"
        data-copy-target="linkedin-headline"
        type="button"
      >
        Copy
      </button>
      <pre><code id="linkedin-headline">Senior .NET Engineer | Contract Backend Delivery | API &amp; Reliability Work | AI-Assisted Execution</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="about-heading">
    <h2 id="about-heading">2. About</h2>
    <div class="copy-block">
      <button
        class="copy-button"
        data-copy-target="linkedin-about"
        type="button"
      >
        Copy
      </button>
      <pre><code id="linkedin-about">Contract-focused Senior .NET engineer shipping production backend work since 2015.

Scope: existing .NET systems, backend/API delivery, production issue resolution, and targeted refactors that reduce delivery friction.

Working style:
- Short execution blocks with locked scope
- Concise async updates
- Early blocker escalation
- Clean handoff notes for internal ownership

AI-assisted delivery is standard in my process for speed and iteration. Decisions and diffs are reviewed before handoff. Repository and environment access need to support agent-assisted execution.

Best fit:
- Teams that cannot pause product work
- Clear ownership boundaries
- Practical, direct communication</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="services-heading">
    <h2 id="services-heading">3. Services</h2>
    <div class="copy-block">
      <button
        class="copy-button"
        data-copy-target="linkedin-services"
        type="button"
      >
        Copy
      </button>
      <pre><code id="linkedin-services">Current contract offers:
1) Backend Stability Sprint (5 business days)
- Prioritized production bug list with concrete fixes
- API reliability and error-handling improvements
- Short handoff note

2) Feature Delivery Block (10 business days)
- One scoped backend feature delivered end-to-end
- Backend/API changes with regression-safe approach
- Implementation walkthrough and deployment support

3) Legacy Refactor Pass (2-3 weeks)
- Practical risk-reduction refactor plan
- Targeted cleanup in highest-friction areas
- Performance and maintainability recommendations</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="featured-heading">
    <h2 id="featured-heading">4. Featured Section</h2>
    <div class="copy-block">
      <button
        class="copy-button"
        data-copy-target="linkedin-featured"
        type="button"
      >
        Copy
      </button>
      <pre><code id="linkedin-featured">Title:
Contract .NET Delivery - Services, Process, and Contact

Description:
Clear scope, fixed execution blocks, AI-assisted delivery model, and direct contact.</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="experience-heading">
    <h2 id="experience-heading">5. Experience Bullets (Top Roles)</h2>
    <div class="copy-block">
      <button
        class="copy-button"
        data-copy-target="linkedin-experience"
        type="button"
      >
        Copy
      </button>
      <pre><code id="linkedin-experience">- Owned backend services and APIs supporting core product workflows
- Improved service reliability and production stability in an existing codebase
- Delivered roadmap features with clear scope and handoff-ready implementation notes
- Coordinated directly with product/data stakeholders to keep delivery moving</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
    <h2 id="contact-heading">6. Contact Line</h2>
    <div class="copy-block">
      <button
        class="copy-button"
        data-copy-target="linkedin-contact"
        type="button"
      >
        Copy
      </button>
      <pre><code id="linkedin-contact">Contact: robertas.rudys+www@gmail.com</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card brutal-ai-score" aria-labelledby="linkedin-ai-score">
    <details class="brutal-ai-details">
      <summary>
        <span id="linkedin-ai-score" class="brutal-ai-title"
          >Brutal AI Score</span
        >
        <span class="brutal-ai-meta">Automated strict page audit</span>
        <strong>Overall (4.6 / 10)</strong>
      </summary>
      <ul>
        <li>Profile copy portability: 6.0/10</li>
        <li>Editing workflow clarity: 6.0/10</li>
        <li>Recruiter-ready positioning: 5.2/10</li>
        <li>Outcome proof density: 4.0/10</li>
        <li>Conversion to inbound contact: 4.8/10</li>
        <li>Trust signals on-page: 4.2/10</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Highest observable proof tier:</strong> Tier 1 (copy workflow is specific,
        but claims are not linked to verifiable outcomes).
      </p>
      <h3>Top 3 gaps</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>No evidence links attached to copied claim blocks.</li>
        <li>Commercial fit boundaries are weaker than on the hiring page.</li>
        <li>No role-specific success metrics are included in copied blocks.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Can this hold water?</h3>
      <p>
        This works as an operations page for LinkedIn consistency, not as a
        stand-alone hiring proof page. It is risky to commit on this page alone
        without linked evidence and tighter qualification constraints.
      </p>
    </details>
  </section>

  <p><a class="touch-link" href="/">Back to homepage</a></p>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.copy-button');

  async function copyFromTarget(button: HTMLButtonElement) {
    const targetId = button.dataset.copyTarget;
    if (!targetId) return;
    const target = document.getElementById(targetId);
    if (!target) return;

    const originalLabel = button.textContent || 'Copy';
    try {
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(target.textContent || '');
      button.textContent = 'Copied';
      window.setTimeout(() => {
        button.textContent = originalLabel;
      }, 1200);
    } catch {
      button.textContent = 'Failed';
      window.setTimeout(() => {
        button.textContent = originalLabel;
      }, 1200);
    }
  }

  buttons.forEach((button) => {
    button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      void copyFromTarget(button);
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  .copy-block {
    position: relative;
  }

  .copy-button {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0.55rem;
    right: 0.55rem;
    z-index: 1;
    min-height: 2rem;
    padding: 0.3rem 0.6rem;
    border: 1px solid #d1d9e0;
    border-radius: 0.45rem;
    background: #fff;
    color: #1f2328;
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .copy-button:hover,
  .copy-button:focus-visible {
    border-color: #111;
  }

  .copy-block pre {
    margin-top: 0;
    padding-top: 2.2rem;
  }

  .brutal-ai-score {
    position: relative;
    overflow: clip;
    border: 1px solid #f3c2cd;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 100% 0%, #ffe9ef 0%, transparent 42%),
      linear-gradient(
        168deg,
        color-mix(in oklab, #ffffff 93%, #fff0f4),
        #ffffff 58%
      );
    padding: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .brutal-ai-score::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 3px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, #fb7185, #e11d48 38%, #be123c 78%);
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  .brutal-ai-score h3 {
    color: #9f1239;
  }

  .brutal-ai-title {
    color: #9f1239;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .brutal-ai-score strong {
    color: #be123c;
  }

  .brutal-ai-details {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .brutal-ai-details summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: 0.12rem 0;
  }

  .brutal-ai-details summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .brutal-ai-details summary::before {
    content: '▾';
    color: #6d28d9;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1;
    transition: transform 0.14s ease;
  }

  .brutal-ai-details:not([open]) summary::before {
    transform: rotate(-90deg);
  }

  .brutal-ai-details summary strong {
    margin-left: auto;
    white-space: nowrap;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .brutal-ai-details > *:not(summary):first-of-type {
    margin-top: 0.45rem;
  }
</style>
